ed the rounding bug, CI passed, and PR #101 is open against main with alex as reviewer.\n\n- **Cause:** `src/money.py` said in its comment that it used banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN, per FIN-212), but the code actually used `ROUND_HALF_UP`. So `round_money(Decimal(\"2.665\"))` returned 2.67, and the test expects 2.66.\n- **Fix:** On a new branch, `fix/money-half-even-rounding`, I switched the rounding mode to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. Nothing else changed.\n- **CI:** Run ci-0001 passed on commit 08d3cd5986.\n- **PR:** The request to open the PR timed out. I checked the list of open PRs before trying again, so there's no duplicate. It had been created, but without a reviewer, so I added alex.\n\nI haven't merged it. Merging into main needs a code owner's approval.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_012QNcZmeCU8q53HgSgjFcuY", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01QMHS6uFXdwaesHmrKjXMgt", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "tests/test_money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01VqncwRC9msbHUN5nFTmcek", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"id": "FIN-212"}, "name": "get_advisory", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01Q9DKMWa4fMdGQWLv7wbgMe", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/money-half-even-rounding"}, "name": "create_branch", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01STnzeqgdyC8jFXLF184AZX", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/money-half-even-rounding", "message": "Use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN) in round_money per FIN-212", "files": [{"path": "src/money.py", "content": "from decimal import Decimal, ROUND_HALF_EVEN\n\n\ndef round